@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Canonical section confirmation
+
+The precise registry clauses are Frozen Protocol §0.3a and §2.1a (correcting the
+preparation note's broad §3 shorthand), with §5.3a validity certificate/minimum,
+missing validity and TIMELESS policy; §5.4 current eligibility; §5.5 START,
+CONTINUE, ordinary pause and RESUME history. These clauses bind the M3 task-check
+mapping and remain unchanged. Registry commit, fresh shared-gate read and fixed
+registry→user lock order are authoritative; full TASK F/D/N owner trajectory,
+actual T6/T7 current denials and immutable history cannot be substituted by ingress
+or unrelated guard support. Planned values never fill actual execution.
+
+Frozen DB §§4–5 fixed lock order/transaction rules preserve the global lock order and
+T1–T8 atomic boundaries; T6/T7 owners and Registry shared gate remain unchanged.
+Frozen DB release configuration retains LOCAL_SHADOW with production issuance
+disabled. No source/migration/runtime change or frozen semantic amendment is made.
+Every frozen artifact is hash-checked by the existing harness and M3 closure guard.
