+Reviewed immutable implementation/result SHA `351f0eda41ad492e66115f9ea1e41e3e0f9abf3d`, protected base `9268fc8dd8c071c02dc5c698274dbf6fcd112776`. Working changes after that SHA were excluded. Recommendation: CHANGES_REQUIRED for the two content-oracle findings recorded in DB_CONCURRENCY.json; both require a new implementation SHA and fresh review.
+
+Read AGENTS.md, indexed authority, HG-044 governance record and M3 closure contract, THREAD_REVIEW contract/schema, and pr-merge-reviewer, db-transaction-reviewer and protocol-guardian skills. Relevant frozen clauses: Protocol sections 2.1a and 8; DB sections 3 command ownership and 4 fixed lock order. Registry gate precedes S01; global revoke commits independently without user lock; T1-T8 remain distinct; external waits remain outside coordination transactions. HG044 changes no runtime, SQL, DB test, migration, command owner, frozen file, requirement set, backlog, traceability, or workflow. No lock order, idempotency, fencing, call-ledger dispatch, replay, production/shadow, or authorization semantic changes were found.
+
+The exit mapping pins 52 full task-check contracts. I01-I09 map actual owner DC selectors with both contender orders required by pinned oracles; PU equality remains separate and I04@WF NOT_RUN. All 31 boundary rows retain exact canonical ledgers: 19 planned executable and 12 deferred, including B04 full reauthorization despite mandatory guard support, B11/B12 PU, B14 WF, and eight E2E rows. Shadow usability and R04 E2E remain NOT_RUN. The synthetic prospective fixture is never real execution evidence. No real M3 instance is created.
+
+Dependency closure recursively reads exact MERGED integrations, verifies reachable result/review/merge SHA provenance and both consumer base/tested ancestry. KL078-to-KL076 and KL079-to-KL077 dependencies remain declared; supporting KL074 retains M1 membership. M1/M2 schema branches/definitions are structurally identical; 70 existing validator functions, including ordinary integration/review provenance, remain byte-identical. Only existing validate and governance_allowed_patterns functions change. Frozen authority hashes and selected implementation capture raw hashes were independently verified.
+
+The fresh integrated regression mechanism requires all 16 merges at one tested SHA, own governance-only suffix, exact ordered commands, hashed regular Git blob stdout/JUnit/collection, positive collection and executed counts, matching testcase identities, no failures/skips/deselection substitutes. The two reproduced findings weaken these checks. Aside from these findings, no additional DB concurrency blocker was identified in this preliminary round. The captured focused 79-pass and harness 869-pass executions are historical implementation evidence at e748b37; this review does not relabel them fresh integrated DB evidence.
+
+Bounded check command, tested SHA, exit code and raw output are retained in audit.json. The content-oracle reproductions execute the immutable Git validator and stub only Git/provenance boundaries using synthetic logs; they prove the defective content predicates, not a successful real closure. No full suite repeat, PostgreSQL lifecycle, foreign namespace, implementation edit, or commit was performed. Applicable unchanged hosted DB/quality CI and entirely fresh reviews at the repaired SHA remain required before normal merge; the user has not authorized actual merge.
