+# M3 mechanical closure contract — HG044
+
+M3 closes the plan's minimal isolated TEST PostgreSQL protocol demonstration. It
+creates no product/release PASS, production activation, executable real-data shadow,
+or reproduced historical model evidence. This contract ratifies the exit mapping;
+a later governance PR may create `docs/exec-plans/milestones/M3.json` only after all
+prerequisites and fresh integrated executions exist. HG044 creates no instance.
+M1/M2 representations and validators retain their existing meaning. An M3 instance
+itself must be an unchanged regular Git blob committed at HEAD; symlinks and ambient
+working-tree substitutes cannot supply a closure. JSON sources reject duplicate keys.
+
+The evaluated full Git commit must contain exactly these active M3 identities:
+`harness-backlog-v0.2/KL-019` through `KL-029`, and `KL-075` through `KL-079` (16).
+The integrations array names each once with its exact regular Git-blob hash. M2
+closure, recursively including its historical M1 prerequisite, must validate at the
+evaluated revision. `supporting_prerequisites` names exactly KL-074, whose membership
+remains M1; its integration is support, never substitution or a historical M1 edit.
+Every transitive declared dependency has a valid MERGED integration. Its merge
+precedes both the consumer result's base and tested commits, including KL078→KL076
+and KL079→KL077. No backlog status or ambient filesystem implies MERGED.
+
+All result, reviewed-head, review-record and merge revisions must be reachable from
+the evaluated revision. The ordinary integration validator supplies exact result
+representation/bytes, schema, PASS checks, tested suffix and required SHA-bound
+review validation, including HG043's exact regular-blob review evidence provenance.
+M3 additionally excludes nonregular integration/result/review records.
+
+The exact executable mapping lives in `M3_EXIT_TASK_CHECKS` in the indexed validator:
+
+| Exit | Integrated task checks and meaning |
+|---|---|
+| full_test_fdn_trajectory_and_repair | KL027 actual full F/D/N owner trajectory to T6/T7 and F2 repair |
+| current_denials_and_immutable_history | KL027 revoke/expiry; KL077 current CONTINUE/RESUME and immutable replay; KL028 B07/B16 lifecycle-valid denials |
+| nine_actual_dc_interleavings | KL026 I01–I09 DC, both ordered contenders, plus separate PU time equality |
+| ready_sealed_barriers | KL023 writer/seal frontier; KL028 B01 PU/DC, B02/B03 READY/SEALED barriers |
+| registry_commit_freshness_and_closure | KL021 committed T2-GLOBAL semantics; KL028 B04 mandatory guard support, B05/B06/B11/B12/B13/B14 support/B15/B17 PU/DC |
+| validity_missing_timeless_and_expiry | KL022 minimum/missing closure and TIMELESS policy, persisted certificate; KL028 B08/B09 PU/DC/B10/B18 |
+| isolated_test_and_evaluation_boundaries | KL027 scope/namespace; KL028 namespace; every named KL029 isolated boundary selector |
+
+Each exit contains an exact duplicate-free task-check set, not arbitrary document
+references. Each witness carries namespaced identity, check ID, PASS, exact command,
+exact result `tested_commit`, canonical JSON SHA256 of `pass_oracle`, result artifact
+and raw evidence `{path, revision, sha256}`. The result artifact and raw log resolve
+at the integrated `reviewed_head_sha`; both are regular Git blobs with exact hashes.
+The command resolves through the result's unique named check and pinned full check
+contract digest. Logs must record positive executed pytest counts, without failures,
+skips, errors, deselection, xfail or xpass substitutes. Historical task logs remain
+historical inputs; none are presented as a fresh integrated regression.
+
+`integrated_regression` is one hashed regular JSON blob at the evaluated revision,
+under the later closure governance ID's evidence directory, named
+`m3-regression-<7..40 hex>.json`. It contains `change_id`, `tested_commit`, `status:
+PASS`, exact ordered `commands: M3_REGRESSION_COMMANDS`, and matching `executions`.
+The command set covers full unit/harness/validation, every mapped selector, all M3
+plain pytest suites, and legacy migrations/transaction-interface DB regression.
+Every execution has command, tested SHA, integer zero exit code and hashed stdout.
+Pytest executions also have hashed JUnit and collection JSON. Raw references within
+this record are `{path, sha256}` bound to the containing evidence revision (no
+self-referential commit IDs). Collection JSON records exact
+`uv run pytest --collect-only -q <selectors>`, tested SHA, integer zero exit, nodeids and
+hashed raw collection stdout. Positive collection counts, raw nodeids and all
+executed JUnit names/counts must agree. Every declared selector must contribute
+at least one collected and executed case; selectors cannot be replaced or omitted.
+All raw files belong to this closure governance evidence directory. No empty,
+skipped, xfail, failed, duplicate or arbitrary-check run can substitute.
+
+The one fresh tested revision contains all 16 task merges, including KL028/KL029.
+Its suffix to evaluated permits only this closure governance record and newly
+appended own evidence under the existing governance-tested suffix rule. Changes to
+code, tests, task artifacts, authorities or bookkeeping of another task stale the
+regression. Use each suite's isolated supported namespace; legacy DB regression can
+use the unchanged isolated hosted lifecycle. Never run a foreign local fixture
+namespace. External waits remain outside coordination transactions.
+
+`boundary_layers` exactly retains KL028's canonical 31-row ledger, including all
+metadata, selectors, oracles and future owners. Only the 19
+`KL028_PLANNED_EXECUTABLE` rows become PASS, backed by the mapped task checks. The 12
+deferred rows remain NOT_RUN, including B04@DC full TEST reauthorization (its guard
+support check is mandatory), eight B@E2E actual API→workflow→DB→eligibility/rendering,
+B11/B12@PU missing pure commit-state evaluator, and B14@WF worker/fault infrastructure.
+`interleaving_layers` contains I01–I09@DC PASS with KL026 named checks and I04@WF
+NOT_RUN with future M4 worker/fault process evidence. Exact PU equality is never PG
+equality; DC never becomes WF/E2E. Ingress, registration and actual T7 denials keep
+their original reach labels. Historical evaluation fixtures are not shadow-owner
+outputs. `shadow_usability_status` and `r04_e2e_status` remain NOT_RUN.
+
+Frozen baseline and every bound frozen file hash must match current frozen
+authority. `product_requirement_pass_claims` is empty;
+`production_auto_activation` and `shadow_executable` are false;
+`historical_model_evidence` stays UNVERIFIED_HISTORICAL_DECLARATION with independent
+reproducibility false. Deferred product/release work remains assigned downstream.
+Closure sequencing requires the minimal TEST evidence above; it introduces no
+M3→M4 or KL029→KL045 dependency cycle and waives no later release requirement.
